# OpenTelemetry: logs + metrics + traces exported via OTLP (env-gated, see
# hub_api/telemetry.py). opentelemetry-exporter-otlp is the umbrella package
# pulling in both grpc and http/protobuf proto exporters so the wire protocol
# is selectable at runtime via OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL. Kept OUT of the
# semgrep scan env on purpose -- semgrep pins opentelemetry-sdk~=1.37.0 and
# runs fully isolated via uvx (scripts/hooks/run-semgrep.sh); never add these
# to a shared/semgrep environment.
# Pinned to the 1.27.0/0.48b0 release line (2024-08-28), NOT latest (1.45.0):
# every opentelemetry-proto release from 1.28.0 onward requires protobuf>=5.0,
# which conflicts with this file's protobuf==4.25.9 pin (gencode in
# proto/**/*_pb2.py is generated against protobuf 4.25.1 -- see the protobuf
# comment above; bumping requires regenerating those committed stubs, out of
# scope here). 1.27.0 is the newest opentelemetry-proto release still on
# protobuf<5.0. Flagged residual: revisit alongside a coordinated
# protobuf/_pb2 stub regen, matching the existing protobuf CVE posture below.
opentelemetry-sdk==1.27.0
opentelemetry-exporter-otlp==1.27.0
opentelemetry-instrumentation-asgi==0.48b0
opentelemetry-instrumentation-sqlalchemy==0.48b0
# opentelemetry-instrumentation==0.48b0 (pulled in by the two instrumentation
# packages above) imports `pkg_resources` at module load; setuptools>=81
# dropped pkg_resources entirely, which would otherwise resolve to the
# unconstrained latest and break the import at startup. Pin to the last 80.x
# release that still ships it.
setuptools<81,>=70
# Prometheus text-exposition /metrics endpoint (existing hub-api
# ServiceMonitor + Grafana dashboards scrape this; OTLP metrics above are the
# secondary/primary OTel signal, this is the Prometheus scrape surface).
